    "text": "```python\ndef starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of the number of n-digit\n    positive integers that that start or end end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, 2 ** n):\n        if i == 1 or i %  10 == 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```\n\nThis function iterates through all possible n-digit numbers (from 1 to \\( 2^n \\)) and counts those that start or end with 1.",
